## Phase 2 — Iteration 3 — BLOCKED then RF-002-03 fix (planner artifact)

- iter-3 generator: BLOCKED on `behavior_contract_breach_known` at first edit. Removing `= DateTime.UtcNow` from Feature.{CreatedAt,UpdatedAt} and FeatureStagePlan.{CreatedAt,UpdatedAt} drifted `feature_entity_shape` by exactly 76 bytes (4 × 19-byte suffixes). The plan's parity claim ("default-initializer expression is NOT part of the public-shape grep") was empirically wrong because `grep -nE` emits the entire matched line, not just the regex span. Generator correctly halted, reverted both files, did not commit. Working tree was clean at HEAD=55cd078 after the block.
- driver: same shape as RF-001-01 — a planner-pinned `exact` byte-parity surface with a brittle grep that captures more than the plan's stated intent.
- assigning new ID: RF-002-03 (the iter-2 evaluator already used RF-002-01 / RF-002-02 for unrelated tooling concerns; the entity-shape fix is iteration-3-discovered and gets the next free numeric).
- change: behavior-capture.json — `feature_entity_shape` capture command now pipes through `sed -E 's/(\}[[:space:]]*)=[[:space:]]*[^;]+;/\1;/'` after the `grep -nE`, which strips the trailing `= <expr>;` default-initializer suffix on the LAST property `}` of each line. This honors the plan's stated intent ("match property declarations, not their default expressions"). Verified via direct shell run: `CreatedAt`, `UpdatedAt` lines lose the `= DateTime.UtcNow` suffix; non-defaulted properties (e.g. `public int Id { get; init; }`) are unaffected.
- baseline re-capture: ran capture-behavior-contract.mjs in a worktree at b96117e with the updated config; replaced gan-harness-refactor/per-request-datetime-provider/behavior-contract.{json,md}. Frozen baseline now holds the suffix-stripped form for the entity-shape surface.
- post-fix sanity: re-captured at HEAD=55cd078 + diffed against new baseline. `feature_entity_shape: no diff`. All other surfaces parity (test_corpus_assertion_count remains the planner-pinned additive parity 969→977).
- recovery: relaunch iter-3 generator with the same slice (entity-init drop + DevFeatureSeeder migration). The block was a planner artifact — generator-side slice is correct.

## Phase 2 — Iteration 3 — RF-002-03 fix v2 (sed pattern correction)

- iter-3 generator REPLAY: BLOCKED again on `feature_entity_shape` drift. The first sed pattern `s/(\}[[:space:]]*)=[[:space:]]*[^;]+;/\1;/` was asymmetric — it captured `}<whitespace>` into \1 then re-inserted `\1;`, producing `} ;` on lines that originally had a default and `}` on lines that didn't. Net: 8-byte loss after default removal because the synthetic `;` disappeared.
- generator's recovery hint was correct: drop the `;` re-insertion. New pattern: `s/(\})[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*[^;]+;/\1/` — replace `}<whitespace>=<expr>;` with `}`. Symmetric: lines with defaults become `}`, lines without defaults stay `}` (no match). Same output before and after default removal.
- baseline re-captured at b96117e a SECOND time with the corrected sed.
- post-fix sanity (probe edit applied + reverted): with default suffixes present at HEAD=55cd078, `feature_entity_shape: no diff` against new baseline. With default suffixes removed (probe), STILL `feature_entity_shape: no diff`. Capture surface is now insensitive to the iter-3 default-removal edit.
- run.log entry pattern: each capture-surface fix gets an explicit log entry so future readers can audit the trail. Three planner artifacts have surfaced over the harness run so far: RF-001-01 (JWT line-number shift), RF-002-03 v1 (entity-shape default suffix capture), RF-002-03 v2 (sed pattern asymmetry). All are byproducts of using `grep -nE` / line-based captures against a code surface that legitimately churns.

